  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "02780e5b-d486-48e7-acc9-d2e4f352d35c",
    "name": "Octobat Coupons Subscriptions API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": {
      "content": "Octobat is a billing, invoicing, and tax-compliance platform for online businesses. This OpenAPI document describes the public REST API at base URL https://apiv2.octobat.com. The API is Stripe-style: resource-oriented, form or JSON request bodies, and HTTP Basic authentication using your secret key as the username with an empty password (curl: -u sk_live_xxx:). Test-mode keys (sk_test_) and live-mode keys (sk_live_) select the environment.\n\nEndpoint provenance: paths marked \"confirmed\" are demonstrated directly in Octobat's own documentation (register-transactions and tax-calculation guides). The remaining CRUD and action paths are modeled from Octobat's official Ruby SDK (github.com/0ctobat/octobat-ruby), which derives resource URLs as the snake_cased, pluralized class name and uses POST to create, PATCH to update, GET to retrieve/list, and DELETE to remove. Request and response schemas are representative, not exhaustive; consult the live API reference at https://v2apidoc.octobat.com for full field-level detail.\n\nOperating status: Octobat was acquired by Mirakl in November 2021. The standalone marketing site now redirects to mirakl.com; docs.octobat.com and apiv2.octobat.com remain available to existing integrators.\n\nContact Support:\n Name: Octobat\n Email: support@octobat.com",
      "type": "text/plain"
    }
  }
